course: dictionary
lesson: 933
title: Blindness: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blindness usually means being unable to see, either completely or almost completely. But words can carry more than one meaning, so check the clues around the word. In «colour blindness», the word tells you the problem is with telling colours apart.
explain: «His blindness to his own mistakes meant he never fixed them.» Here blindness does not mean you cannot see. It means not noticing or not understanding something, even when it is there. The clue is «his own mistakes»: he could see them, but he did not notice them.
explain: Some phrases name a specific kind of blindness. «Colour blindness» means finding some colours hard to tell apart, often red and green. «Snow blindness» means eye damage from strong light. Each phrase tells you what kind it is, so read the whole phrase, not just the first word.
fact: Blindness means being unable to see, either completely or almost completely.
fact: Blindness to something means not noticing or not understanding it, as in «his blindness to his own mistakes».
fact: «Colour blindness» means some colours are hard to tell apart, often red and green. About 1 in 12 men of European descent have red-green colour blindness, and most colour-blind people still see many colours.
fact: «Snow blindness» is eye damage caused by UV light. Fresh snow reflects up to about 80% of the sun's UV light, even on cloudy days.
fact: Respect matters: many blind people use a white cane, a guide dog or Braille. Offer help, ask first, and never pat a working guide dog.
exercise: «His blindness to his own mistakes meant he never fixed them.» What does blindness mean here? | Being very tired | Being unable to see at all | A type of snow | *Not noticing or not understanding something
exercise: Which phrase means some colours are hard to tell apart? | Braille | *Colour blindness | Guide dog | Snow blindness
exercise: «Fresh snow reflects up to about 80% of the sun's UV light, and UV can burn the surface of the eye, called snow blindness.» Find and copy the phrase that names the eye damage. | *snow blindness | fresh snow | UV light | colour blindness
test: Blind people may use a white cane, a guide dog or Braille. What is Braille? | A kind of snow | A sound made by a cane | Large printed letters for easy reading | *Raised dots read with the fingers
test: «Missing something in plain sight because your attention is elsewhere is called inattentional blindness.» What does this describe? | Being unable to see at all | *Missing something in plain sight because your attention is elsewhere | Being unable to see colours | Eye damage from strong sunlight
exam: Which sentence uses blindness with its meaning of not noticing something? | The room was dark, so she could not see the desk | *He was blind to the warning sign and walked straight past it | Red and green looked the same to him | Fresh snow is bright and cold
